---
term: Exit
section: evolution-and-protection
order: 100
definition: A member's right to leave a corporation under its exit procedure.
seeAlso:
  - anti-capture-protection
  - member
  - dissolution
---
Exit is a [[fundamental protections|Level 0 protection]]. It keeps corporations accountable, because members who are poorly served can withdraw their participation and, where the charter allows, their contributions.
